#: ../../source/arduino_start/03_create_save.rst:16
msgid "How to create, open or Save the Sketch?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/03_create_save.rst:19
msgid "When you open the Arduino IDE for the first time or create a new sketch, you will see a page like this, where the Arduino IDE creates a new file for you, which is called a \"sketch\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/03_create_save.rst:23
msgid "These sketch files have a regular temporary name, from which you can tell the date the file was created. ``sketch_oct14a.ino`` means October 14th first sketch, ``.ino`` is the file format of this sketch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/03_create_save.rst:25
msgid "Now let's try to create a new sketch. Copy the following code into the Arduino IDE to replace the original code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/03_create_save.rst:45
msgid "Press ``Ctrl+S`` or click **File** -> **Save**. The Sketch is saved in: ``C:\\Users\\{your_user}\\Documents\\Arduino`` by default, you can rename it or find a new path to save it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/03_create_save.rst:49
msgid "After successful saving, you will see that the name in the Arduino IDE has been updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/arduino_start/03_create_save.rst:53
msgid "Please continue with the next section to learn how to upload this created sketch to your Arduino board."
msgstr ""
